    <!--
      The ORCHESTRATION read model, over agt_ops and nothing else. It is family-agnostic on
      purpose: AGT's bounded context is "launch every family's stages and record what happened",
      so a view grouping by launch_intent.stage spans CRR, PRR and MRR without crossing a database
      boundary. That is the one genuinely cross-family surface rpt owns, and it costs no join
      across databases because AGT already holds the fact in one place.

      [!CONVENTION-OVERRIDE] Canon is that a service owns its own database and no other
      (https://microservices.io/patterns/data/database-per-service.html). rpt creates the rpt
      schema inside agt_ops, which is AGT's database. These views are AGT's read model and their
      correct home is AGT. They live here because rpt already carries the session-identity and
      grants discipline they need; the migration to AGT is specified in the SCRUM-107 report and
      is an AGT change, not an rpt one.
    -->

